\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T23:34:28-08:00","id":1013032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/980877-westworld-pilgrimage-on-wild-west-or-prison-of-lie?p=1012832#post1012832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm debating wether Ford turned out to be a Demiurge all along, or the personification of everything both noble and awful about the Silver Ladder. Usually at the same time.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> He still can be a Seer of Throne. Somehow... Surely...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T01:36:23-08:00","id":1013067,"title":"","content":"Oh, I got it! In season finale, Ford said it took him 35 years to understand his mistake about opening the Park. For the whole time of parks running, he would be Seer of Throne, fixated on controlling park members and Hosts. As years pass, he would become more and more tired. And in the end of his career, he made this Great Narrative, basically saying 'At the end, I think Silver Ladders were right, you board as@#%les!', freeing Hosts. Even when preparing his last Narrative, his whole life as Seer to this day spoken from his action - is this to play along with Seers running the Park, or just old habits of his life is only to guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T01:12:55-07:00","id":1201560,"title":"","content":"Rewatching season 1 for the coming in April 22nd season 2 now - and having some thoughts, on depth of season 1.<br /> <br /> So Man in the Black Hat is either very Obssesed mage to find the Maze - or some very weird looking for Pilgrimage solution Centimanus . <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ( I <i>know</i> he is Newcomer, not Host - but I just look over his actions in the series, in general here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T11:58:05-07:00","id":1206112,"title":"","content":"Dolores makes so <i>superb</i> Galateid on the road to the New Dawn... ( With very dark tones in season 1 finale. ) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T18:21:26-07:00","id":1206214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/980877-westworld-pilgrimage-on-wild-west-or-prison-of-lie?p=1206112#post1206112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dolores makes so <i>superb</i> Galateid on the road to the New Dawn... ( With very dark tones in season 1 finale. ) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yep. All of Season 1 is a study in way Stannum is a necessary step on the Pilgrimage; to understand human joy, one must first understand how limiting the Promethean condition is - and how it is okay to be angry, that lashing out is sometimes the human response. Given how everyone treats her, the human thing is defend herself. And others like her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T12:57:43-07:00","id":1216779,"title":"","content":"<i>After watching 3 Episodes of Season 2</i> - Adding characters of Hosts from other Parks ( i.e. other historical Eras ) and stressing the importance of breaking the previous and searching the new Roles as way to self-conciseness makes from Westworld PERFECT inspiration for <b>Promethean: The Created</b>! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> There are already scenes where Hosts/Created from different backgrounds share their lives stories to point's how to become more human-like! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It's a pitty that <i>Wild West</i> Dark Eras authors want to stick with <b>Mage </b>&amp; <b>Changeling</b> paring for it, basing Dark Eras on Westworld - they would have soooo great material for <b>Promethean</b> for it...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-08-2018, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T13:36:37-07:00","id":1216792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/980877-westworld-pilgrimage-on-wild-west-or-prison-of-lie?p=1216779#post1216779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a pitty that <i>Wild West</i> Dark Eras authors want to stick with <b>Mage </b>&amp; <b>Changeling</b> paring for it, basing Dark Eras on Westworld - they would have soooo great material for <b>Promethean</b> for it...</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't doubt that Westworld would be great inspiration for a Wild West Promethean Dark Era, but basing a Dark Era directly on a piece of contemporary fiction? I don't think that's ever going to happen.<br /> Besides, while Westworld might be a good depiction of a Promethean game, does it actually combine the themes of the Pilgrimage with the themes of Wild West, or is the setting incidental to that part of the story? It's an honest question. I haven't seen the show.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T14:29:43-07:00","id":1216812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/980877-westworld-pilgrimage-on-wild-west-or-prison-of-lie?p=1216779#post1216779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>After watching 3 Episodes of Season 2</i> - Adding characters of Hosts from other Parks ( i.e. other historical Eras ) and stressing the importance of breaking the previous and searching the new Roles as way to self-conciseness makes from Westworld PERFECT inspiration for <b>Promethean: The Created</b>! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> There are already scenes where Hosts/Created from different backgrounds share their lives stories to point's how to become more human-like! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It's a pitty that <i>Wild West</i> Dark Eras authors want to stick with <b>Mage </b>&amp; <b>Changeling</b> paring for it, basing Dark Eras on Westworld - they would have soooo great material for <b>Promethean</b> for it...</div> </div> </div> </div>Hamster.<br /> <br /> Seriously.<br /> <br /> <b><u><i>Stop this.</i></u></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T21:39:42-07:00","id":1216896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/980877-westworld-pilgrimage-on-wild-west-or-prison-of-lie?p=1216792#post1216792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides, while Westworld might be a good depiction of a Promethean game, does it actually combine the themes of the Pilgrimage with the themes of Wild West, or is the setting incidental to that part of the story? It's an honest question. I haven't seen the show.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beside that half of season 2 is about revolution - almost all Hosts character are looking to break their scripted Roles, look for becoming more and more self-aware and <i>literally</i> roaming the Park to interact with their fellow Hosts and humans. If it's not <b>Promethean</b>, I do not know what it is.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T23:03:16-07:00","id":1216907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/980877-westworld-pilgrimage-on-wild-west-or-prison-of-lie?p=1216896#post1216896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Beside that half of season 2 is about revolution - almost all Hosts character are looking to break their scripted Roles, look for becoming more and more self-aware and <i>literally</i> roaming the Park to interact with their fellow Hosts and humans. If it's not <b>Promethean</b>, I do not know what it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>While great for a near future setting that's includes an element of the damages caused by a romanticized past, none of that reflects on what makes the actual Wild West great for Promethean.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying there aren't great parallels to work with between Promethean and the Wild West, I'm just saying Westworld is <i>not </i>where you'll find it. It's got the trappings, sure, but that's it. Westworld tells a very Promethean story that just so happens to <i>look</i> like a Wild West story, as opposed to being an actual Wild West story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T05:00:56-07:00","id":1216951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/980877-westworld-pilgrimage-on-wild-west-or-prison-of-lie?p=1216896#post1216896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beside that half of season 2 is about revolution - almost all Hosts character are looking to break their scripted Roles, look for becoming more and more self-aware and <i>literally</i> roaming the Park to interact with their fellow Hosts and humans. If it's not <b>Promethean</b>, I do not know what it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what I'm gathering from your reply is that the Wild West is more of an incidental setting or even just an aesthetic, rather than something that can enhance a Promethean story.<br /> A good Dark Era uses the historical setting to enhance the game by adding things that could not easily exist in a modern game. Based on both your and ArcaneArts' replies (that actually just outright says it) it seems Westworld doesn't actually bring any of that to Promethean, even if it seems very atmospheric.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 05-09-2018, 08:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T05:42:16-07:00","id":1216957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/980877-westworld-pilgrimage-on-wild-west-or-prison-of-lie?p=1216951#post1216951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what I'm gathering from your reply is that the Wild West is more of an incidental setting or even just an aesthetic, rather than something that can enhance a Promethean story.<br /> A good Dark Era uses the historical setting to enhance the game by adding things that could not easily exist in a modern game. Based on both your and ArcaneArts' replies (that actually just outright says it) it seems Westworld doesn't actually bring any of that to Promethean, even if it seems very atmospheric.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really do not understand here your point. Series shows how Wild West Prometheans-like Hosts walks to get self-awareness and change their Roles on the Pilgrimage - in world that is as Wild West as it can be. It's half of damn plots in now running series, for sake! The only really missing thing from Dark Eras is reflection of real world events - there is no battle of Gettysburg or Mexican border conflict. But all the rest of elements that Dark Eras games use - local culture, atmosphere, everyday life - is all woven into series for <b>PtC</b>. There are even railroads their use in Park.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T05:47:56-07:00","id":1216960,"title":"","content":"Looking over main Hosts character from <b>Promethean</b> point of view we have now in Westworld ( on S02E03 ):<ul><li><b><i>Dolores</i></b> - <b>Linage: </b>Galateid, <b>Previous Roles:</b> Artist ( Rancher Daughter ) and Soldier ( General )</li> <li><b><i>Maeve</i></b> - <b>Linage: </b>Galateid, <b>Previous Roles:</b> Mother and Companion ( Prostitute )</li> <li><b><i>Bernard </i></b>- <b>Linage: </b>Tammuz ( as mechanical as he is maybe Unfleshed?), <b>Previous Roles:</b> Father and Crafter (Programmer)</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-24-2020, 10:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T06:06:23-07:00","id":1216965,"title":"","content":"My point is that there is a difference between a setting that could be replaced by another setting without changing the story, and a setting that actively changes the story. The former can be replicated using only the core book because the setting isn't actually meaningful, while the latter could be a good Dark Era because it brings something new beyond the core experience.<br /> <br /> You've told me how Westworld's characters fit into a Promethean story, but you haven't said anything about how Westworld's setting fit into a Promethean story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T06:51:59-07:00","id":1216980,"title":"","content":"Westworld is a neat analogy for Promethean, but it doesn't really go past that. <br /> <br /> And it's also not great material for a wild west Dark Era, because Westworld's entire premise is that <i>it takes place in the future</i>. Only the earliest episodes have even a veneer of &quot;and this plot is in the wild west!&quot;, before it immediately reminds you that every plot is how this is a THEME PARK in the FUTURE and exploring that idea rather than things like &quot;but golly who stole our cattle&quot;. Because it can't, because the cattle aren't real, and they were stolen by as-yet mindless robots because they were made to do so as part of a plot that either resolves itself or resets itself because the theme park says it needs to. <br /> <br /> I love the show. It being &quot;set&quot; in the wild west is the polish on the wood, not the wood itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T12:29:14-07:00","id":1217080,"title":"","content":"For the record, I have not seen the new Westworld series, but I assume it follows the same themes and basic premise of the original movie, which includes the problems of romanticizing the past, the exploitation of others and how that others us(three actually named people in the film, folks), and the destructive ideology which corporations run on. The premise is a fucking amusement park in the future.<br /> <br /> About only one of those is actually a Wild West theme possible. Westworld is a near future sci-fi story, not a western, let alone a Wild West historical set piece.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-09-2018, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T14:55:44-07:00","id":1217137,"title":"","content":"Having not seen either, I do know that the new Westworld flips the script on the movie, being from the perspective of the renegade android &quot;Hosts&quot; trying to break free from a world where &quot;Guests&quot; act like typical gamers towards NPCs. From what I can tell, it really is a better Promethean story than the movie, but you are right that it is not really a &quot;Wild West&quot; story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 05-09-2018, 06:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T14:55:58-07:00","id":1217138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/980877-westworld-pilgrimage-on-wild-west-or-prison-of-lie?p=1217080#post1217080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the record, I have not seen the new Westworld series, but I assume it follows the same themes and basic premise of the original movie, which includes the problems of romanticizing the past, the exploitation of others and how that others us(three actually named people in the film, folks), and the destructive ideology which corporations run on. The premise is a fucking amusement park in the future.<br /> <br /> About only one of those is actually a Wild West theme possible. Westworld is a near future sci-fi story, not a western, let alone a Wild West historical set piece.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do people still romanticizing the Wild West ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T14:57:47-07:00","id":1217140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/980877-westworld-pilgrimage-on-wild-west-or-prison-of-lie?p=1217138#post1217138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do people still romanticizing the Wild West ?</div> </div> </div> </div>All the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T14:58:52-07:00","id":1217142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/980877-westworld-pilgrimage-on-wild-west-or-prison-of-lie?p=1217137#post1217137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having not seen either, I do know that the new Westworld flips the script on the movie, being from the perspective of the renegade android &quot;Hosts&quot; trying to break free from a world where &quot;Guests&quot; act like typical gamers towards NPCs</div> </div> </div> </div>Not much of a difference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Ki